# Read-only RPC + bounded offline EIP-712 vouchers. This file does not authorize deployment or funding.
AF_MARKET_ORIGIN=https://your-approved-host.example
AF_MARKET_PORT=4101
AF_MARKET_DATA_DIR=/absolute/private/new-fair-launch-storage
AF_MARKET_WEB_ROOT=/absolute/path/apps/web/dist
# Leave the manifest unset to expose NOT_DEPLOYED and disable all asset operations.
# AF_MARKET_MANIFEST=/absolute/private/verified-market-manifest.json
# AF_MARKET_RPC_URL=https://your-approved-robinhood-testnet-provider.example
# Existing Google-verified access service DB; readonly. Native/demo login cannot claim.
# Prefer the bounded Unix socket when the authentication DB has a separate service owner.
# Exactly one identity transport may be configured. Socket directory: auth UID, market group, 0710;
# socket: same owner/group, 0660. The market service does not need database read permissions.
# AF_ACCESS_IDENTITY_SOCKET=/run/alphaforge-identity/identity.sock
# AF_ACCESS_IDENTITY_DB=/absolute/private/access.sqlite
# Separate owner-controlled 0600 files containing offline EIP-712 keys; never deployer EOA keys.
# AF_MARKET_QUOTE_SIGNER_FILE=/absolute/private/quote-signer.key
# AF_MARKET_CLAIM_SIGNER_FILE=/absolute/private/claim-signer.key
# Alternatively decrypt separate existing encrypted keys only in memory; never write a plaintext copy.
# For each signer use either SIGNER_FILE or the paired KEYSTORE_FILE / UNLOCK_FILE, never both.
# All files must be service-owned, 0600, single-link regular files in non-writable private directories.
# AF_MARKET_QUOTE_KEYSTORE_FILE=/absolute/private/quote.keystore.json
# AF_MARKET_QUOTE_UNLOCK_FILE=/absolute/private/quote.unlock
# AF_MARKET_CLAIM_KEYSTORE_FILE=/absolute/private/claim.keystore.json
# AF_MARKET_CLAIM_UNLOCK_FILE=/absolute/private/claim.unlock
